+# Provisioning approvers for cosign sign-blob via KMS
+
+1) Decide approver model: each approver gets an identity that can request a short-lived signing grant (recommended) rather than raw KMS key access.
+2) Workflow (recommended):
+   - Create a small signing service with an approval workflow in front of KMS that only signs approved blobs for authorized approvers.
+   - Alternatively, create a key in KMS that approvers can use via cosign sign-blob with IAM/OIDC restrictions (least privileges, narrow scope).
+3) For tests, approvers can use local cosign keypair:
+   - cosign generate-key-pair
+   - cosign sign-blob --key cosign.key approval.json --output-signature approval.sig
+4) Store approver public keys or KMS key policy ARNs in ops secrets so review-queue can verify via cosign verify-blob.
